      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — using named constants, hex notation to clarify byte values and the expected little-endian assembly, and a cleaner structure.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored test replaces the opaque inline arithmetic expression with a named `littleEndianBytes` array using hex literals and a clearly named `expectedValue = 0x80040302L`, making the little-endian byte-to-long assembly immediately obvious to readers."
